summary:
  Re-fetch all saves a 16 px favicon or Google's icon over a logo the row
  already has.

history:
  The button promises to keep a logo it cannot better, and a tab-sized find
  replaced a 1024 px logo the listener had set. A find of logoRank 4 never
  replaces a logo now.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FaviconLogic.js

find:
      if (webUrlOrEmpty(current) !== "" && best.url === current) return false;

replace:
      if (false) return false;

expect:
  Killed by tst_faviconlogic::test_a_tab_icon_never_replaces_a_logo_a_row_has.
  Line-neutral.
